name 'pl-aif1-js-functions-clean-code'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Why Does Code Need to Be Clean?</h1>

Last lesson was about storing and updating values with variables. This lesson is about something different: how the code around those variables gets organized.

Before diving into functions, it helps to see what "clean" actually means, since it's not just a matter of taste.

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;">
<p>📖 <b>Clean Code</b> is code that's organized, consistently formatted, and easy for another person, or AI, to read and modify.</p>
</div>
<br>
<p>Here's the same three lines of code written two ways:</p>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 20px 0;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 220px;">
    <div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: #E0762A; margin-bottom: 8px;">NOT CLEAN</div>
    <div style="background-color: #2B2745; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: #E4E2F8; line-height: 1.8;">
let n = 5;<br>let Score=n+10;<br>scoreDisplay.textContent=Score;
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 220px;">
    <div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: #1FA34D; margin-bottom: 8px;">CLEAN</div>
    <div style="background-color: #2B2745; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: #E4E2F8; line-height: 1.8;">
let baseScore = 5;<br>let finalScore = baseScore + 10;<br>scoreDisplay.textContent = finalScore;
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

Both versions do exactly the same thing. The clean version just uses **names that describe** what each value actually is, and **formats consistently**, so anyone reading it, including AI, can follow along without guessing.

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<p><strong>💡 Teacher tip:</strong> if students give a vague answer like "messy code is bad," push them to name a specific consequence, a bug, a slowdown, a moment AI misunderstood something.</p>
</div>

---

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
